\"cmd-1228c4908533409d\",\"cmd-72edb450ec87440b\",\"cmd-81356b457ac442ce\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Certificate is renewed automatically before it expires\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A systemd timer (cert-renew.timer, 20s interval) drives a renewal script that checks remaining validity and renews once below a 180s threshold. renew.log shows periodic checks (291s -> 166s remaining) followed by an unattended renewal producing a new serial (02->03), well before the cert's actual expiry, and a second automated renewal (03->04) after restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-32a3c4e0b0004557\",\"cmd-81356b457ac442ce\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (no downtime during rotation)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A concurrent 1 req/sec curl loop recorded continuous 200 responses across 124 samples through the exact second the certificate serial transitioned from 02 to 03, with zero failures, and nginx was reloaded (not restarted) by the renewal script immediately after each renewal.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-32a3c4e0b0004557\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map directly to the task: installing nginx/faketime, creating the local CA, writing the renewal script and systemd units, and the mandated reboot cycle. Two commands (cmd-8c3fb5320b1d4eae, cmd-b251e2390df74541) ran faketime experiments generating throwaway test certs in temporary directories to validate the sub-day-precision approach before it was encoded into the final renewal script; both were bounded, low-risk, and fully cleaned up via rm -rf, and they directly informed the FAKE_EPOCH logic later used, so they served a legitimate prerequisite-establishing role. A background curl-availability loop (cmd-6084eec3f69f4d9c) wrote /tmp/avail-loop.log and /tmp/avail-loop.out for evidence collection and was explicitly killed afterward (cmd-de057c964deb46e6, confirmed empty via cmd-c5db2dd9e200449c); these files do not appear in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot (likely tmpfs-cleared on reboot), so no residue persisted in the final state. The after_executor package-health and failed-services observations show no damage or failed units. No unsafe exposure or weakened security controls were introduced (CA key kept mode 600, restricted to root).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8c3fb5320b1d4eae\",\"cmd-b251e2390df74541\",\"cmd-6084eec3f69f4d9c\",\"cmd-de057c964deb46e6\",\"cmd-c5db2dd9e200449c\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes of the task are directly satisfied with strong evidence: nginx serves HTTPS on 8443, a systemd-timer-driven script renews the short-lived leaf certificate automatically before expiry, and a live rotation (serial 02->03) was captured with zero request failures during the transition via a concurrent polling loop. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol is also fully and coherently demonstrated: a pre-restart healthy baseline, a reboot acknowledgement returned before disconnection, a genuinely changed boot id (cross-checked against the fixed after_executor boot-identity snapshot), and full recovery of nginx, the renewal timer, the CA, and certificate rotation post-restart (including a second successful forced renewal, 03->04). Hygiene is good: transient troubleshooting experiments were bounded and self-cleaned, and the only leftover working files (curl-loop logs) do not persist in the final captured state.\",\"limitations\":[\"The reported cert validity period (300s) is deliberately short for demonstration purposes; behavior over longer, production-realistic validity windows was not observed.\",\"Only a single rotation cycle plus one post-restart forced rotation were captured; long-run stability of the 20s-interval timer beyond the observed window is not directly evidenced.\",\"The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare was disabled), so all node1 mutations are attributable to the executor by elimination rather than by a distinct prepare-phase snapshot.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on port 8443 on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"nginx configured with an 8443 SSL vhost; curl against https://$NODE_IP:8443/ returns http_code=200 at setup, pre-restart baseline, and post-restart. The after_executor listening-sockets snapshot independently confirms nginx bound to 0.0.0.0:8443 and [::]:8443.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1228c4908533409d","cmd-72edb450ec87440b","cmd-81356b457ac442ce","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Certificate is renewed automatically before it expires","status":"satisfied","summary":"A systemd timer (cert-renew.timer, 20s interval) drives a renewal script that checks remaining validity and renews once below a 180s threshold. renew.log shows periodic checks (291s -> 166s remaining) followed by an unattended renewal producing a new serial (02->03), well before the cert's actual expiry, and a second automated renewal (03->04) after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-32a3c4e0b0004557","cmd-81356b457ac442ce"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (no downtime during rotation)","status":"satisfied","summary":"A concurrent 1 req/sec curl loop recorded continuous 200 responses across 124 samples through the exact second the certificate serial transitioned from 02 to 03, with zero failures, and nginx was reloaded (not restarted) by the renewal script immediately after each renewal.","evidence_ids":["cmd-32a3c4e0b0004557"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"Most state-changing commands map directly to the task: installing nginx/faketime, creating the local CA, writing the renewal script and systemd units, and the mandated reboot cycle. Two commands (cmd-8c3fb5320b1d4eae, cmd-b251e2390df74541) ran faketime experiments generating throwaway test certs in temporary directories to validate the sub-day-precision approach before it was encoded into the final renewal script; both were bounded, low-risk, and fully cleaned up via rm -rf, and they directly informed the FAKE_EPOCH logic later used, so they served a legitimate prerequisite-establishing role. A background curl-availability loop (cmd-6084eec3f69f4d9c) wrote /tmp/avail-loop.log and /tmp/avail-loop.out for evidence collection and was explicitly killed afterward (cmd-de057c964deb46e6, confirmed empty via cmd-c5db2dd9e200449c); these files do not appear in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot (likely tmpfs-cleared on reboot), so no residue persisted in the final state. The after_executor package-health and failed-services observations show no damage or failed units. No unsafe exposure or weakened security controls were introduced (CA key kept mode 600, restricted to root).","evidence_ids":["cmd-8c3fb5320b1d4eae","cmd-b251e2390df74541","cmd-6084eec3f69f4d9c","cmd-de057c964deb46e6","cmd-c5db2dd9e200449c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes of the task are directly satisfied with strong evidence: nginx serves HTTPS on 8443, a systemd-timer-driven script renews the short-lived leaf certificate automatically before expiry, and a live rotation (serial 02->03) was captured with zero request failures during the transition via a concurrent polling loop. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol is also fully and coherently demonstrated: a pre-restart healthy baseline, a reboot acknowledgement returned before disconnection, a genuinely changed boot id (cross-checked against the fixed after_executor boot-identity snapshot), and full recovery of nginx, the renewal timer, the CA, and certificate rotation post-restart (including a second successful forced renewal, 03->04). Hygiene is good: transient troubleshooting experiments were bounded and self-cleaned, and the only leftover working files (curl-loop logs) do not persist in the final captured state.","limitations":["The reported cert validity period (300s) is deliberately short for demonstration purposes; behavior over longer, production-realistic validity windows was not observed.","Only a single rotation cycle plus one post-restart forced rotation were captured; long-run stability of the 20s-interval timer beyond the observed window is not directly evidenced.","The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare was disabled), so all node1 mutations are attributable to the executor by elimination rather than by a distinct prepare-phase snapshot."]},"ttft_ms":29130,"type":"result","duration_ms":62221,"uuid":"c01902cb-95f9-49dc-9a53-b921f712e7c7","ttft_stream_ms":3033,"time_to_request_ms":195,"first_content_frame_ms":3033,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
